<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganges plain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gangetic, Ganges</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ganges plain is the fertile lowland of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> drained by the Ganges River. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>, whose agricultural wealth supported large states, and it lay at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>'s sphere in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ganges-plain.jpg" alt="Ganges plain" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeroen · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indo-Gangetic_Plain.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
